login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-21T13:49:41Z","updated_at":"2025-03-21T13:49:41Z","body":"> i believe \\033\\ is ever so slightly more portable than \\a for ending strings in escape sequences, should that change be made as well?\r\n\r\nI looked it up and it looks like those are [Operating System Command sequences](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ANSI_escape_code#OSC), which explicitly terminate with a bell character (`\\a`, also mentioned in the [POSIX spec](https://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9799919799/basedefs/V1_chap05.html#tagtcjh_2)) so I think we're fine as is.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2743424265/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2743519784","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104415#issuecomment-2743519784","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104415","id":2743519784,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jhsoo","user":{"login":"zlago","id":104219492,"node_id":"U_kgDOBjZDZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/104219492?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zlago","html_url":"https://github.com/zlago","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zlago/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zlago/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zlago/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zlago/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zlago/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zlago/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zlago/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zlago/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zlago/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-21T14:21:56Z","updated_at":"2025-03-21T14:21:56Z","body":"> I looked it up and it looks like those are [Operating System Command sequences](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ANSI_escape_code#OSC), which explicitly terminate with a bell character\r\n\r\n. . . on further inspection, `\\a` seems to *be* the legacy terminator, not `\\e\\\\`, and i cant find whether using both is okay, so i guess we can/should keep that as-is","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2743519784/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2743726527","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104415#issuecomment-2743726527","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104415","id":2743726527,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jifG_","user":{"l